From: Tao Gong <gongtao0607@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 22 Aug 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: mt76: mt7996: fix struct mt7996_mcu_wed_rro_ba_delete_event layout

Correct the definition of struct mt7996_mcu_wed_rro_ba_delete_event to
match the 12-byte event record layout sent by firmware. The size mismatch
previously resulted in misaligned event parsing when processing batch BA
session deletions.

The UNI_WED_RRO_BA_SESSION_DELETE handler in mt7996_mcu_wed_rro_event()
walks a batch of these records, striding by sizeof(*e) and reading
e->session_id from each. With the struct 4 bytes too short, every record
after the first is read at the wrong offset, so garbage session ids get
queued onto dev->wed_rro.poll_list and recycled by dev->wed_rro.work,
corrupting HW_RRO session bookkeeping. The sibling status struct
mt7996_mcu_wed_rro_ba_event already carries wlan_id/tid/__rsv1 in the
same position, confirming the true firmware layout.

Signed-off-by: Tao Gong <gongtao0607@gmail.com>
---
--- a/mt7996/mcu.h
+++ b/mt7996/mcu.h
@@ -284,6 +284,9 @@ struct mt7996_mcu_wed_rro_ba_delete_event {
 	__le16 len;

 	__le16 session_id;
+	__le16 wlan_id;
+	u8 tid;
+	u8 __rsv1;
 	u8 __rsv2[2];
 } __packed;

